/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · Joshua chapters 1-5
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("joshua", [
{n:1, name:"Be Strong and Courageous", seal:{ref:"Joshua 1:9",verse:"Have not I commanded thee? Be strong and of a good courage; be not afraid, neither be thou dismayed: for the LORD thy God is with thee whithersoever thou goest."},
 facts:["Did you know that 'be strong and of a good courage' is spoken three times to Joshua in chapter 1, by God and by the people? Repetition in Scripture signals urgency, and this charge became Israel's rallying cry.",
 "Did you know Joshua had already served Moses as his minister for decades, yet God still had to command him personally? Obedience to a great leader is no substitute for hearing God's own voice.",
 "Did you know the land promise in chapter 1 stretches from the wilderness to Lebanon and from the Euphrates to the great sea? That is far more territory than Israel ever fully possessed."],
 questions:[
  {q:"After whose death does God speak to Joshua in Joshua 1?", options:["Moses","Aaron","Joseph","Miriam"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 1:1",verse:"Now after the death of Moses the servant of the LORD it came to pass, that the LORD spake unto Joshua the son of Nun, Moses’ minister, saying,",
   insight:"Joshua steps in only after Moses is dead. God moves His work forward with new servants in every generation."},
  {q:"What title does God give to Moses in Joshua 1:1?", options:["My servant","My prophet","My chosen","My friend"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 1:1",verse:"Now after the death of Moses the servant of the LORD it came to pass, that the LORD spake unto Joshua the son of Nun, Moses’ minister, saying,",
   insight:"God's highest praise for Moses is simply 'my servant.' Titles from heaven honor obedience, not office."},
  {q:"Whom does Joshua command as soon as he receives God's charge?", options:["The officers of the people","The priests alone","The two spies","The tribal elders"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 1:10",verse:"Then Joshua commanded the officers of the people, saying,",
   insight:"Joshua acts at once on what God said. Prompt obedience is the first fruit of hearing God's voice."},
  {q:"What is the very first command God gives Joshua in Joshua 1:2?", options:["Arise","Pray","Wait","Sacrifice"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 1:2",verse:"Moses my servant is dead; now therefore arise, go over this Jordan, thou, and all this people, unto the land which I do give to them, even to the children of Israel.",
   insight:"Grief must give way to action. God begins the new chapter of Joshua's life with one word: Arise."},
  {q:"Which river must Israel cross to enter the promised land?", options:["Jordan","Euphrates","Nile","Red Sea"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 1:2",verse:"Moses my servant is dead; now therefore arise, go over this Jordan, thou, and all this people, unto the land which I do give to them, even to the children of Israel.",
   insight:"The Jordan stands between Israel and the promise. Every inheritance of faith has a river to cross first."},
  {q:"How much of the land would God give, according to Joshua 1:3?", options:["Every place that the sole of your foot shall tread upon","Only the valleys of Canaan","As far as Joshua could see","The east bank of Jordan only"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 1:3",verse:"Every place that the sole of your foot shall tread upon, that have I given unto you, as I said unto Moses.",
   insight:"God's promise measured possession by treading. The ground they walked in faith became theirs."},
  {q:"What is the western boundary of the promised land in Joshua 1:4?", options:["The great sea","The Red Sea","The Dead Sea","The Nile"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 1:4",verse:"From the wilderness and this Lebanon even unto the great river, the river Euphrates, all the land of the Hittites, and unto the great sea toward the going down of the sun, shall be your coast.",
   insight:"The 'great sea' is the Mediterranean. God's gift to Israel had wide borders, wider than they ever claimed."},
  {q:"What is the eastern boundary mentioned in Joshua 1:4?", options:["The river Euphrates","The Tigris","The Jordan","The Sea of Galilee"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 1:4",verse:"From the wilderness and this Lebanon even unto the great river, the river Euphrates, all the land of the Hittites, and unto the great sea toward the going down of the sun, shall be your coast.",
   insight:"The Euphrates marked the far edge of the promise. God's vision for Israel reached beyond the Jordan valley."},
  {q:"What promise does God make about Joshua's enemies in Joshua 1:5?", options:["No man shall be able to stand before thee all the days of thy life","The nations will flee before hearing thy name","Jericho will fall in one day","The kings will surrender without battle"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 1:5",verse:"There shall not any man be able to stand before thee all the days of thy life: as I was with Moses, so I will be with thee: I will not fail thee, nor forsake thee.",
   insight:"No enemy could stand before Joshua because God stood with him. Strength is measured by company, not by courage alone."},
  {q:"What personal promise does God repeat to Joshua in Joshua 1:5?", options:["I will be with thee","I will bless thy children","I will lengthen thy days","I will give thee riches"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 1:5",verse:"There shall not any man be able to stand before thee all the days of thy life: as I was with Moses, so I will be with thee: I will not fail thee, nor forsake thee.",
   insight:"Before any strategy, God gives Joshua His presence. 'I will be with thee' is the sum of every promise."},
  {q:"How many times is the charge 'be strong and of a good courage' spoken in this chapter?", options:["Three","Once","Twice","Five"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 1:9",verse:"Have not I commanded thee? Be strong and of a good courage; be not afraid, neither be thou dismayed: for the LORD thy God is with thee whithersoever thou goest.",
   insight:"The charge is repeated because courage leaks. What God repeats, we should remember."},
  {q:"What must Joshua observe in order to prosper, according to Joshua 1:7?", options:["All the law which Moses commanded","The customs of the nations","His own wisdom","The advice of the elders"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 1:7",verse:"Only be thou strong and very courageous, that thou mayest observe to do according to all the law, which Moses my servant commanded thee: turn not from it to the right hand or to the left, that thou mayest prosper whithersoever thou goest.",
   insight:"Success comes from keeping all the law, not part of it. Partial obedience cannot carry a whole promise."},
  {q:"In which direction must Joshua not turn, according to Joshua 1:7?", options:["To the right hand or to the left","Toward the sea or the mountains","East or west","Up or down"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 1:7",verse:"Only be thou strong and very courageous, that thou mayest observe to do according to all the law, which Moses my servant commanded thee: turn not from it to the right hand or to the left, that thou mayest prosper whithersoever thou goest.",
   insight:"The law's path is straight. Turning aside in either direction leads off the road to blessing."},
  {q:"What is to be done with the book of the law, according to Joshua 1:8?", options:["It shall not depart out of thy mouth","It shall be kept in the ark","It shall be taught only to the priests","It shall be hidden in the camp"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 1:8",verse:"This book of the law shall not depart out of thy mouth; but thou shalt meditate therein day and night, that thou mayest observe to do according to all that is written therein: for then thou shalt make thy way prosperous, and then thou shalt have good success.",
   insight:"The law belongs in Joshua's mouth, not just his heart. Speaking God's word rehearses it for battle."},
  {q:"How often is Joshua to meditate on the book of the law?", options:["Day and night","Every Sabbath","Each new moon","Once a year"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 1:8",verse:"This book of the law shall not depart out of thy mouth; but thou shalt meditate therein day and night, that thou mayest observe to do according to all that is written therein: for then thou shalt make thy way prosperous, and then thou shalt have good success.",
   insight:"Day and night meditation means the word frames his whole life. Courage is fed by constant feeding on Scripture."},
  {q:"What do the people promise Joshua in Joshua 1:17?", options:["We will hearken unto thee in all that thou commandest us","We will cross the Jordan first","We will build thee a house","We will number the tribes"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 1:17",verse:"According as we hearkened unto Moses in all things, so will we hearken unto thee: only the LORD thy God be with thee, as he was with Moses.",
   insight:"The people pledge full obedience to Joshua as they did to Moses. God-given leaders deserve a wholehearted following."},
  {q:"Why should Joshua not be afraid, according to Joshua 1:9?", options:["The LORD thy God is with thee whithersoever thou goest","He has forty thousand soldiers","Jericho's walls are weak","Moses left detailed plans"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 1:9",verse:"Have not I commanded thee? Be strong and of a good courage; be not afraid, neither be thou dismayed: for the LORD thy God is with thee whithersoever thou goest.",
   insight:"Fear is answered not by strength but by presence. God with us, everywhere we go, makes fear unreasonable."},
  {q:"What do the officers order the people to prepare within three days?", options:["Victuals, for they will cross the Jordan","Weapons for the siege","Tents for a long wait","Bridges over the river"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 1:11",verse:"Pass through the host, and command the people, saying, Prepare you victuals; for within three days ye shall pass over this Jordan, to go in to possess the land, which the LORD your God giveth you to possess it.",
   insight:"They prepare food for the march, not a siege. Faith crosses the river before the river is crossed."},
  {q:"How soon will Israel cross the Jordan, according to Joshua 1:11?", options:["Within three days","Within a month","After the harvest","When the river is low"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 1:11",verse:"Pass through the host, and command the people, saying, Prepare you victuals; for within three days ye shall pass over this Jordan, to go in to possess the land, which the LORD your God giveth you to possess it.",
   insight:"Three days means soon, not someday. God's promises often carry a deadline that calls for readiness."},
  {q:"Which tribes must send armed men across ahead of their brothers?", options:["Reuben, Gad, and half the tribe of Manasseh","Dan and Naphtali","Judah and Benjamin","Levi and Simeon"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 1:14",verse:"Your wives, your little ones, and your cattle, shall remain in the land which Moses gave you on this side Jordan; but ye shall pass before your brethren armed, all the mighty men of valour, and help them;",
   insight:"The tribes already settled must still fight for their brothers. A blessing received early is a debt owed to others."}
 ]},
{n:2, name:"Rahab and the Spies", seal:{ref:"Joshua 2:11",verse:"And as soon as we had heard these things, our hearts did melt, neither did there remain any more courage in any man, because of you: for the LORD your God, he is God in heaven above, and in earth beneath."},
 facts:["Did you know Rahab is listed in the genealogy of Jesus in Matthew 1, alongside Ruth? The Canaanite harlot of Jericho became an ancestor of the Messiah.",
 "Did you know the spies were hidden under stalks of flax spread on Rahab's roof? Flax was laid out to dry for making linen, so the roof was a natural hiding place.",
 "Did you know James uses Rahab as his great example of faith shown by works? He pairs her with Abraham in James 2, a surprising honor roll."],
 questions:[
  {q:"What do the two spies do after coming down from the mountain?", options:["They return to Joshua and tell him all things that befell them","They enter Jericho again at night","They hide in a cave for a week","They send a messenger ahead"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 2:23",verse:"So the two men returned, and descended from the mountain, and passed over, and came to Joshua the son of Nun, and told him all things that befell them:",
   insight:"The spies bring back a full report, not rumors. Faithful witnesses tell all that befell them, nothing hidden."},
  {q:"What does Rahab do after the spies depart?", options:["She binds the scarlet line in the window","She flees the city at once","She tells her neighbors everything","She burns the flax on the roof"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 2:21",verse:"And she said, According unto your words, so be it. And she sent them away, and they departed: and she bound the scarlet line in the window.",
   insight:"She binds the scarlet line immediately. Faith that waits for a better time is faith that never acts."},
  {q:"What word is told to the king of Jericho in Joshua 2:2?", options:["Men of Israel came in hither tonight to search out the country","Israel has crossed the Jordan","The spies have been captured","Rahab has betrayed the city"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 2:2",verse:"And it was told the king of Jericho, saying, Behold, there came men in hither to night of the children of Israel to search out the country.",
   insight:"News of the spies reaches the king at once. God's work in a place always stirs the powers of that place."},
  {q:"In whose house do the spies lodge in Jericho?", options:["Rahab's","The king's","The gatekeeper's","An innkeeper's"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 2:1",verse:"And Joshua the son of Nun sent out of Shittim two men to spy secretly, saying, Go view the land, even Jericho. And they went, and came into an harlot’s house, named Rahab, and lodged there.",
   insight:"God's mission runs through Rahab's house. No address is too dark for God's plan to visit."},
  {q:"What is Rahab called in Joshua 2:1?", options:["An harlot","A widow","A merchant","A princess"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 2:1",verse:"And Joshua the son of Nun sent out of Shittim two men to spy secretly, saying, Go view the land, even Jericho. And they went, and came into an harlot’s house, named Rahab, and lodged there.",
   insight:"Scripture names Rahab honestly, yet she is honored for her faith. God saves real people with real pasts."},
  {q:"Who demands that Rahab hand over the spies?", options:["The king of Jericho","The elders of Jericho","The captain of the guard","The priests of Baal"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 2:3",verse:"And the king of Jericho sent unto Rahab, saying, Bring forth the men that are come to thee, which are entered into thine house: for they be come to search out all the country.",
   insight:"Even the king of Jericho hears of the spies. Nothing done for God stays hidden from the enemy for long."},
  {q:"What lie does Rahab tell the king's messengers?", options:["The men went out before the gate was shut, and she did not know where they went","They never came to her house","They left at dawn for the mountains","They crossed the Jordan at night"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 2:4",verse:"And the woman took the two men, and hid them, and said thus, There came men unto me, but I wist not whence they were:",
   insight:"Rahab's quick lie protects the spies. Her imperfect faith is counted righteous because it acted."},
  {q:"Where does Rahab hide the two spies?", options:["Under stalks of flax on the roof","In a grain cellar","Behind the city gate","In a well outside the wall"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 2:6",verse:"But she had brought them up to the roof of the house, and hid them with the stalks of flax, which she had laid in order upon the roof.",
   insight:"Flax drying on the roof became a hiding place. Ordinary details of life often shelter God's servants."},
  {q:"When does Rahab come up to the roof to speak with the spies?", options:["Before they were laid down","After midnight","At dawn","During the feast"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 2:8",verse:"And before they were laid down, she came up unto them upon the roof;",
   insight:"She goes up before they sleep, urgent with her request. Faith does not wait for a convenient hour."},
  {q:"What does Rahab say has fallen upon the people of Jericho?", options:["Terror","Plague","Famine","Darkness"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 2:9",verse:"And she said unto the men, I know that the LORD hath given you the land, and that your terror is fallen upon us, and that all the inhabitants of the land faint because of you.",
   insight:"Terror of the LORD already fills Jericho before one Israelite crosses the river. God goes ahead of His people."},
  {q:"What does Rahab confess about the LORD in Joshua 2:11?", options:["He is God in heaven above, and in earth beneath","He is stronger than the gods of Jericho","He will be king of Canaan","He has forgotten His people"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 2:11",verse:"And as soon as we had heard these things, our hearts did melt, neither did there remain any more courage in any man, because of you: for the LORD your God, he is God in heaven above, and in earth beneath.",
   insight:"A Canaanite woman preaches better theology than many Israelites. True confession knows God rules heaven and earth."},
  {q:"What 'true token' does Rahab ask the spies to give her?", options:["A sign that they will save her father's household alive","A gold bracelet","A written promise","A seal of the king"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 2:12",verse:"Now therefore, I pray you, swear unto me by the LORD, since I have shewed you kindness, that ye will also shew kindness unto my father’s house, and give me a true token:",
   insight:"She asks a 'true token,' not just a promise. Faith looks for assurance it can hold in the hand."},
  {q:"What kindness does Rahab ask the spies to show her?", options:["To save alive her father, mother, brethren, and sisters","To make her queen of Jericho","To give her gold from the spoils","To take her to Israel"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 2:13",verse:"And that ye will save alive my father, and my mother, and my brethren, and my sisters, and all that they have, and deliver our lives from death.",
   insight:"Rahab's faith reaches for her whole family. Genuine conversion always wants the household saved too."},
  {q:"What oath do the spies make to Rahab?", options:["Our life for yours","Our swords for yours","Our homes for yours","Our gold for yours"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 2:14",verse:"And the men answered her, Our life for yours, if ye utter not this our business. And it shall be, when the LORD hath given us the land, that we will deal kindly and truly with thee.",
   insight:"They pledge their own lives for hers. God's servants back their promises with everything."},
  {q:"How does Rahab get the spies out of the city?", options:["She lets them down by a cord through the window","She hides them in a grain cart","She bribes the gate guard","She opens a secret tunnel"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 2:15",verse:"Then she let them down by a cord through the window: for her house was upon the town wall, and she dwelt upon the wall.",
   insight:"A cord through the window becomes an escape route. God often delivers through the humblest means."},
  {q:"Why could Rahab let the spies down through her window?", options:["Her house was upon the town wall","She lived by the city gate","The wall was low there","The guards were asleep"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 2:15",verse:"Then she let them down by a cord through the window: for her house was upon the town wall, and she dwelt upon the wall.",
   insight:"Her house sat on the wall, the very place of Jericho's strength. What the city trusted became God's doorway."},
  {q:"How long do the spies hide in the mountain?", options:["Three days","Seven days","One night","Forty days"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 2:16",verse:"And she said unto them, Get you to the mountain, lest the pursuers meet you; and hide yourselves there three days, until the pursuers be returned: and afterward may ye go your way.",
   insight:"Three days of hiding let the pursuers give up and go home. Patience often outlasts pursuit."},
  {q:"What must Rahab bind in her window so the spies will spare her household?", options:["This line of scarlet thread","A white cloth","A golden cord","A bronze chain"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 2:18",verse:"Behold, when we come into the land, thou shalt bind this line of scarlet thread in the window which thou didst let us down by: and thou shalt bring thy father, and thy mother, and thy brethren, and all thy father’s household, home unto thee.",
   insight:"The scarlet cord marks her window like the blood marked Israel's doors in Egypt. A red thread of mercy runs through Scripture."},
  {q:"What happens to Rahab if she tells of the spies' business?", options:["The spies will be quit of their oath","She will be stoned","Her household will die","She will be enslaved"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 2:20",verse:"And if thou utter this our business, then we will be quit of thine oath which thou hast made us to swear.",
   insight:"The oath binds her to silence. Every covenant of grace carries a call to keep faith with it."},
  {q:"What do the spies report to Joshua about the land?", options:["The LORD hath delivered into our hands all the land","Jericho is too strong to take","We need more spies","The people are willing to surrender"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 2:24",verse:"And they said unto Joshua, Truly the LORD hath delivered into our hands all the land; for even all the inhabitants of the country do faint because of us.",
   insight:"Their report is pure confidence: God has delivered the land. Faith's spies see enemies, but report God's promise."}
 ]},
{n:3, name:"Crossing the Jordan", seal:{ref:"Joshua 3:17",verse:"And the priests that bare the ark of the covenant of the LORD stood firm on dry ground in the midst of Jordan, and all the Israelites passed over on dry ground, until all the people were passed clean over Jordan."},
 facts:["Did you know the Jordan was at flood stage when Israel crossed? Joshua 3:15 says the river overflows all its banks at harvest time, making the miracle far greater.",
 "Did you know the people had to keep about two thousand cubits, nearly half a mile, between themselves and the ark? That distance kept the holy procession visible to all.",
 "Did you know the waters piled up at a town called Adam, far upstream? The damming happened out of sight, and the riverbed simply ran dry where Israel stood."],
 questions:[
  {q:"Where does Israel lodge the night before crossing the Jordan?", options:["At Jordan","At Shittim","At Gilgal","At Jericho"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 3:1",verse:"And Joshua rose early in the morning; and they removed from Shittim, and came to Jordan, he and all the children of Israel, and lodged there before they passed over.",
   insight:"They lodge at the Jordan itself, face to face with the barrier. Faith often camps overnight beside the impossible."},
  {q:"How long do the officers go through the camp before the crossing?", options:["After three days","After seven days","After one night","After forty days"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 3:2",verse:"And it came to pass after three days, that the officers went through the host;",
   insight:"Three days of waiting precede the crossing. God's delays are part of the plan, not a denial."},
  {q:"What are the people to follow when they see it set out?", options:["The ark of the covenant","The pillar of fire","The standard of Judah","The twelve stones"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 3:3",verse:"And they commanded the people, saying, When ye see the ark of the covenant of the LORD your God, and the priests the Levites bearing it, then ye shall remove from your place, and go after it.",
   insight:"They follow the ark, not a map. When God moves, the people move; the presence leads the way."},
  {q:"Who carries the ark before the people?", options:["The priests the Levites","The elders of Israel","The captains of the army","The heads of households"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 3:3",verse:"And they commanded the people, saying, When ye see the ark of the covenant of the LORD your God, and the priests the Levites bearing it, then ye shall remove from your place, and go after it.",
   insight:"Priests, not soldiers, lead the march. Worship goes first when God fights for His people."},
  {q:"How much space must the people keep between themselves and the ark?", options:["About two thousand cubits","About five hundred cubits","About one hundred cubits","About ten thousand cubits"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 3:4",verse:"Yet there shall be a space between you and it, about two thousand cubits by measure: come not near unto it, that ye may know the way by which ye must go: for ye have not passed this way heretofore.",
   insight:"The gap keeps the ark visible to every eye. Reverence gives God room to be seen."},
  {q:"Why must the people follow the ark, according to Joshua 3:4?", options:["That ye may know the way by which ye must go, for ye have not passed this way heretofore","To prove their courage","To count the priests","To stay in formation"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 3:4",verse:"Yet there shall be a space between you and it, about two thousand cubits by measure: come not near unto it, that ye may know the way by which ye must go: for ye have not passed this way heretofore.",
   insight:"They had never passed this way before. New ground requires following God closely, not guessing."},
  {q:"What does Joshua command the people to do in Joshua 3:5?", options:["Sanctify yourselves","Arm yourselves","Build an altar","Fast for a day"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 3:5",verse:"And Joshua said unto the people, Sanctify yourselves: for to morrow the LORD will do wonders among you.",
   insight:"Sanctify yourselves comes before the wonder. God does miracles among people who prepare their hearts."},
  {q:"What will the LORD do among them tomorrow?", options:["Wonders","Signs in the sun","Thunder from heaven","Fire on the altar"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 3:5",verse:"And Joshua said unto the people, Sanctify yourselves: for to morrow the LORD will do wonders among you.",
   insight:"Tomorrow's wonders depend on today's sanctifying. Holiness is the doorway through which power walks."},
  {q:"What will magnifying Joshua cause the people to know?", options:["That as I was with Moses, so I will be with thee","That Joshua is greater than Moses","That the wars will end soon","That the priests are holy"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 3:7",verse:"And the LORD said unto Joshua, This day will I begin to magnify thee in the sight of all Israel, that they may know that, as I was with Moses, so I will be with thee.",
   insight:"God magnifies Joshua so the people will trust God's presence in him. Leaders are exalted to point to God, not themselves."},
  {q:"What are the priests bearing the ark commanded to do at the Jordan?", options:["Stand still in Jordan","Throw stones into the river","Sound the trumpet","Step back from the water"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 3:8",verse:"And thou shalt command the priests that bear the ark of the covenant, saying, When ye are come to the brink of the water of Jordan, ye shall stand still in Jordan.",
   insight:"Stand still in the Jordan: obedience means walking into the water before it parts. Faith steps first."},
  {q:"How many nations will the LORD drive out before Israel, according to Joshua 3:10?", options:["Seven","Three","Ten","Twelve"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 3:10",verse:"And Joshua said, Hereby ye shall know that the living God is among you, and that he will without fail drive out from before you the Canaanites, and the Hittites, and the Hivites, and the Perizzites, and the Girgashites, and the Amorites, and the Jebusites.",
   insight:"Seven nations, a complete number, will be driven out. God's promise covers every enemy, not just some."},
  {q:"Which of these is NOT among the nations named in Joshua 3:10?", options:["Egyptians","Canaanites","Hittites","Amorites"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 3:10",verse:"And Joshua said, Hereby ye shall know that the living God is among you, and that he will without fail drive out from before you the Canaanites, and the Hittites, and the Hivites, and the Perizzites, and the Girgashites, and the Amorites, and the Jebusites.",
   insight:"The Egyptians are not in the land; the seven named are all Canaan's peoples. God's promise names the real opposition."},
  {q:"What title is given to the ark in Joshua 3:11?", options:["The ark of the Lord of all the earth","The ark of the God of battles","The ark of the covenant of war","The ark of the holy mountain"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 3:11",verse:"Behold, the ark of the covenant of the Lord of all the earth passeth over before you into Jordan.",
   insight:"He is 'Lord of all the earth,' not just Israel's God. The ark's power flows from His universal Lordship."},
  {q:"How many men, one from each tribe, must be chosen?", options:["Twelve","Two","Seven","Seventy"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 3:12",verse:"Now therefore take you twelve men out of the tribes of Israel, out of every tribe a man.",
   insight:"Twelve men, one per tribe, share in what is coming. Every tribe owns a part of the memorial."},
  {q:"When will the waters of Jordan be cut off?", options:["As soon as the soles of the feet of the priests rest in the waters","When Joshua lifts his rod","After the people pray all night","When the sun rises"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 3:13",verse:"And it shall come to pass, as soon as the soles of the feet of the priests that bear the ark of the LORD, the Lord of all the earth, shall rest in the waters of Jordan, that the waters of Jordan shall be cut off from the waters that come down from above; and they shall stand upon an heap.",
   insight:"The water parts only when the priests' feet rest in it. God waits for the step of obedience before He moves the obstacle."},
  {q:"What condition was the Jordan in at crossing time?", options:["It overflowed all its banks all the time of harvest","It was at its lowest ebb","It was frozen over","It was fordable on foot"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 3:15",verse:"And as they that bare the ark were come unto Jordan, and the feet of the priests that bare the ark were dipped in the brim of the water, (for Jordan overfloweth all his banks all the time of harvest,)",
   insight:"The river was at flood stage. God chose the hardest moment, so no one could say the crossing was natural."},
  {q:"Near which city did the waters stand up in a heap?", options:["Adam","Jericho","Gilgal","Ai"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 3:16",verse:"That the waters which came down from above stood and rose up upon an heap very far from the city Adam, that is beside Zaretan: and those that came down toward the sea of the plain, even the salt sea, failed, and were cut off: and the people passed over right against Jericho.",
   insight:"The damming happened at Adam, far upstream and out of sight. God's greatest works are often done beyond our view."},
  {q:"What did the waters of the Jordan do, according to Joshua 3:16?", options:["Stood and rose up upon an heap","Turned back toward the mountains","Dried up in a single moment","Froze into a bridge of ice"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 3:16",verse:"That the waters which came down from above stood and rose up upon an heap very far from the city Adam, that is beside Zaretan: and those that came down toward the sea of the plain, even the salt sea, failed, and were cut off: and the people passed over right against Jericho.",
   insight:"The waters stood in a heap like walls. The same God who walled the Red Sea walls the Jordan."},
  {q:"How long did the priests stand firm on dry ground in the Jordan?", options:["Until all the people were passed clean over","For one hour","Until sunset","For three days"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 3:17",verse:"And the priests that bare the ark of the covenant of the LORD stood firm on dry ground in the midst of Jordan, and all the Israelites passed over on dry ground, until all the people were passed clean over Jordan.",
   insight:"The priests hold their ground until the last Israelite crosses. Leaders stay in the dangerous place until everyone is safe."},
  {q:"What was the riverbed like where Israel crossed?", options:["Dry ground","Mud and reeds","Deep and swift","Rocky and uneven"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 3:17",verse:"And the priests that bare the ark of the covenant of the LORD stood firm on dry ground in the midst of Jordan, and all the Israelites passed over on dry ground, until all the people were passed clean over Jordan.",
   insight:"The riverbed was dry ground, not mud. God does not half dry the river; His miracles are complete."}
 ]},
{n:4, name:"Twelve Memorial Stones", seal:{ref:"Joshua 4:24",verse:"That all the people of the earth might know the hand of the LORD, that it is mighty: that ye might fear the LORD your God for ever."},
 facts:["Did you know the stones were carried from the very middle of the Jordan, where the priests' feet had stood? The memorial came from the place of the miracle itself.",
 "Did you know there were actually two piles of twelve stones? One was set up at Gilgal, and Joshua also set twelve stones in the middle of the Jordan where they stand to this day.",
 "Did you know the stones' purpose was to start conversations with children? The memorial was designed so that when a child asks 'what mean ye by these stones,' the father tells the story of the crossing."],
 questions:[
  {q:"When does God speak to Joshua about the twelve men?", options:["When all the people were clean passed over Jordan","Before the crossing began","During the night march","After Jericho fell"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 4:1",verse:"And it came to pass, when all the people were clean passed over Jordan, that the LORD spake unto Joshua, saying,",
   insight:"God speaks the moment the crossing is complete. Instruction follows obedience; the next step comes after the last one is taken."},
  {q:"How many men is Joshua to take, one from each tribe?", options:["Twelve","Two","Seven","Ten"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 4:2",verse:"Take you twelve men out of the people, out of every tribe a man,",
   insight:"Twelve men again, tribe by tribe. In God's people, no tribe is left out of the remembering."},
  {q:"From where are the twelve men to take the stones?", options:["Out of the midst of Jordan, from the place where the priests' feet stood firm","From the banks of the river","From the mountains nearby","From the quarry at Jericho"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 4:3",verse:"And command ye them, saying, Take you hence out of the midst of Jordan, out of the place where the priests’ feet stood firm, twelve stones, and ye shall carry them over with you, and leave them in the lodging place, where ye shall lodge this night.",
   insight:"The stones come from the miracle's exact spot. Memorials should be quarried from the place where God acted."},
  {q:"How many stones is each man to carry?", options:["One stone upon his shoulder","Two stones in his arms","Three stones in a basket","As many as he can lift"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 4:5",verse:"And Joshua said unto them, Pass over before the ark of the LORD your God into the midst of Jordan, and take ye up every man of you a stone upon his shoulder, according unto the number of the tribes of the children of Israel:",
   insight:"One stone per man, carried on the shoulder. Remembering is personal work; each man bears his own share."},
  {q:"What will the stones be, according to Joshua 4:6?", options:["A sign among you","A boundary marker","An altar for sacrifice","A throne for Joshua"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 4:6",verse:"That this may be a sign among you, that when your children ask their fathers in time to come, saying, What mean ye by these stones?",
   insight:"The stones are a sign, not a shrine. They point away from themselves to what God did."},
  {q:"When children ask about the stones, what are fathers to tell them?", options:["That the waters of Jordan were cut off before the ark of the covenant","That the stones fell from heaven","That giants carried them","That Moses commanded it"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 4:7",verse:"Then ye shall answer them, That the waters of Jordan were cut off before the ark of the covenant of the LORD; when it passed over Jordan, the waters of Jordan were cut off: and these stones shall be for a memorial unto the children of Israel for ever.",
   insight:"The answer is a story, not a slogan. Children learn faith when parents narrate God's acts."},
  {q:"What are the stones to be for the children of Israel?", options:["A memorial for ever","A playground","A place of judgment","A treasury"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 4:7",verse:"Then ye shall answer them, That the waters of Jordan were cut off before the ark of the covenant of the LORD; when it passed over Jordan, the waters of Jordan were cut off: and these stones shall be for a memorial unto the children of Israel for ever.",
   insight:"A memorial for ever means the story outlives the eyewitnesses. Some stones preach longer than the men who set them."},
  {q:"Where do the twelve men lay the stones down that night?", options:["In the lodging place where they lodged","At the foot of Mount Nebo","Beside the ark","Outside the camp gate"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 4:8",verse:"And the children of Israel did so as Joshua commanded, and took up twelve stones out of the midst of Jordan, as the LORD spake unto Joshua, according to the number of the tribes of the children of Israel, and carried them over with them unto the place where they lodged, and laid them down there.",
   insight:"They lay the stones down in their lodging place. The memorial begins in the camp's daily life, not in a museum."},
  {q:"Where else does Joshua set up twelve stones?", options:["In the midst of Jordan, in the place where the feet of the priests stood","On the top of Mount Ebal","At the gates of Jericho","In the tabernacle courtyard"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 4:9",verse:"And Joshua set up twelve stones in the midst of Jordan, in the place where the feet of the priests which bare the ark of the covenant stood: and they are there unto this day.",
   insight:"A second pile stays in the riverbed, hidden by the returning waters. Some memorials are for God's eyes alone."},
  {q:"How long do those stones in the Jordan remain, according to Joshua 4:9?", options:["Unto this day","For forty years","Until the exile","For one generation"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 4:9",verse:"And Joshua set up twelve stones in the midst of Jordan, in the place where the feet of the priests which bare the ark of the covenant stood: and they are there unto this day.",
   insight:"'Unto this day' marks an eyewitness record. The writer expects readers to check the stones themselves."},
  {q:"Why did the priests stand in the Jordan, according to Joshua 4:10?", options:["Until every thing was finished that the LORD commanded Joshua","Until the sun stood still","Until the enemy fled","Until the sacrifices were burned"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 4:10",verse:"For the priests which bare the ark stood in the midst of Jordan, until every thing was finished that the LORD commanded Joshua to speak unto the people, according to all that Moses commanded Joshua: and the people hasted and passed over.",
   insight:"They stood until everything commanded was finished. Faithful leaders hold position until the whole work is done."},
  {q:"How did the people cross, according to Joshua 4:10?", options:["The people hasted and passed over","The people marched in silence","The people sang as they crossed","The people carried the children first"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 4:10",verse:"For the priests which bare the ark stood in the midst of Jordan, until every thing was finished that the LORD commanded Joshua to speak unto the people, according to all that Moses commanded Joshua: and the people hasted and passed over.",
   insight:"The people hasted. When God opens the way, lingering is as faithless as refusing."},
  {q:"Which tribes passed over armed before the children of Israel?", options:["The children of Reuben, Gad, and half the tribe of Manasseh","The children of Judah and Benjamin","The children of Dan and Naphtali","The children of Levi and Simeon"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 4:12",verse:"And the children of Reuben, and the children of Gad, and half the tribe of Manasseh, passed over armed before the children of Israel, as Moses spake unto them:",
   insight:"The settled tribes keep their word and march first into danger. A promise made east of Jordan is kept west of it."},
  {q:"About how many armed men passed over to the plains of Jericho?", options:["Forty thousand","Ten thousand","One hundred thousand","Five thousand"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 4:13",verse:"About forty thousand prepared for war passed over before the LORD unto battle, to the plains of Jericho.",
   insight:"About forty thousand crossed ready for war. They come prepared, though God will fight the battle."},
  {q:"What did the LORD do for Joshua on that day?", options:["He magnified Joshua in the sight of all Israel","He gave him the crown of Canaan","He made him a prophet","He lengthened his life"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 4:14",verse:"On that day the LORD magnified Joshua in the sight of all Israel; and they feared him, as they feared Moses, all the days of his life.",
   insight:"God magnified Joshua publicly, and the people feared him as they feared Moses. Honor from God settles authority."},
  {q:"What does God command the priests bearing the ark to do?", options:["Come ye up out of Jordan","Go down into the river","Sound the trumpet","Divide the people"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 4:16",verse:"Command the priests that bear the ark of the testimony, that they come up out of Jordan.",
   insight:"'Come up out of Jordan' closes the miracle. The priests who entered first leave last; leaders bookend the work."},
  {q:"What happens when the priests' feet touch the dry land?", options:["The waters of Jordan returned unto their place and flowed over all his banks","The river parted again","The stones were washed away","The ark floated downstream"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 4:18",verse:"And it came to pass, when the priests that bare the ark of the covenant of the LORD were come up out of the midst of Jordan, and the soles of the priests’ feet were lifted up unto the dry land, that the waters of Jordan returned unto their place, and flowed over all his banks, as they did before.",
   insight:"The waters return only after the last foot lifts. God's miracles stay in place until His people are safe."},
  {q:"On what day of the month did Israel come up out of Jordan?", options:["The tenth day of the first month","The fourteenth day of the first month","The first day of the second month","The fifteenth day of the seventh month"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 4:19",verse:"And the people came up out of Jordan on the tenth day of the first month, and encamped in Gilgal, in the east border of Jericho.",
   insight:"The tenth day of the first month: four days before Passover. The crossing is timed to the calendar of redemption."},
  {q:"Where did Israel encamp after crossing the Jordan?", options:["In Gilgal, in the east border of Jericho","In Shittim","On Mount Ebal","In the plains of Moab"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 4:19",verse:"And the people came up out of Jordan on the tenth day of the first month, and encamped in Gilgal, in the east border of Jericho.",
   insight:"Gilgal becomes the base camp for the conquest. New beginnings need a home address."},
  {q:"Where does Joshua set up the twelve stones?", options:["In Gilgal","In the Jordan","At Shittim","On Mount Gerizim"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 4:20",verse:"And those twelve stones, which they took out of Jordan, did Joshua pitch in Gilgal.",
   insight:"The public memorial stands at Gilgal, where every generation will pass it. Visible stones start visible conversations."}
 ]},
{n:5, name:"Gilgal: Circumcised and Fed", seal:{ref:"Joshua 5:15",verse:"And the captain of the LORD’S host said unto Joshua, Loose thy shoe from off thy foot; for the place whereon thou standest is holy. And Joshua did so."},
 facts:["Did you know 'Gilgal' means 'rolling,' and God named the place for rolling away the reproach of Egypt? The name itself is a sermon on grace removing shame.",
 "Did you know the manna stopped the very day after Israel ate the produce of Canaan? For forty years God fed them from heaven; then ordinary harvest took over, and that was a blessing.",
 "Did you know the Commander of the LORD's army tells Joshua to remove his sandal, exactly as God told Moses at the burning bush? The holy ground of Exodus meets the holy war of Joshua."],
 questions:[
  {q:"Whose hearts melted when they heard the LORD had dried up the Jordan?", options:["The kings of the Amorites and all the kings of the Canaanites","The king of Egypt","The Philistines","The king of Babylon"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 5:1",verse:"And it came to pass, when all the kings of the Amorites, which were on the side of Jordan westward, and all the kings of the Canaanites, which were by the sea, heard that the LORD had dried up the waters of Jordan from before the children of Israel, until we were passed over, that their heart melted, neither was there spirit in them any more, because of the children of Israel.",
   insight:"Enemy kings lose heart before Israel fires a shot. God disarms opposition before the battle begins."},
  {q:"What does the LORD command Joshua to make in Joshua 5:2?", options:["Sharp knives","Bronze shields","Iron chariots","Stone tablets"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 5:2",verse:"At that time the LORD said unto Joshua, Make thee sharp knives, and circumcise again the children of Israel the second time.",
   insight:"Sharp knives for circumcision, not swords for war. Before fighting Canaan, Israel must be marked as God's people."},
  {q:"What is Joshua to do a second time?", options:["Circumcise again the children of Israel","Number the people again","Cross the Jordan again","Build the tabernacle again"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 5:2",verse:"At that time the LORD said unto Joshua, Make thee sharp knives, and circumcise again the children of Israel the second time.",
   insight:"'Again' signals renewal of the covenant sign. Each generation must own the covenant for itself."},
  {q:"What is the name of the hill where Joshua circumcised the people?", options:["The hill of the foreskins","The hill of the covenant","The hill of witness","The hill of the knives"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 5:3",verse:"And Joshua made him sharp knives, and circumcised the children of Israel at the hill of the foreskins.",
   insight:"The blunt name marks an honest memorial. God does not pretty up the acts that seal His covenant."},
  {q:"Why had the wilderness generation not been circumcised?", options:["Because they walked forty years in the wilderness and the old generation died","Because Moses forbade it","Because there were no knives","Because they forgot the covenant"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 5:4",verse:"And this is the cause why Joshua did circumcise: All the people that came out of Egypt, that were males, even all the men of war, died in the wilderness by the way, after they came out of Egypt.",
   insight:"Forty years of wandering left the sign neglected. Disobedience has a way of suspending covenant obedience."},
  {q:"How long did the children of Israel walk in the wilderness?", options:["Forty years","Thirty years","Seventy years","Twelve years"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 5:6",verse:"For the children of Israel walked forty years in the wilderness, till all the people that were men of war, which came out of Egypt, were consumed, because they obeyed not the voice of the LORD: unto whom the LORD sware that he would not shew them the land, which the LORD sware unto their fathers that he would give us, a land that floweth with milk and honey.",
   insight:"Forty years until the unbelieving generation was consumed. Time itself was God's instrument of judgment."},
  {q:"Why did that generation not see the promised land?", options:["Because they hearkened not unto the voice of the LORD","Because they were too few","Because the land was too far","Because Moses led them wrong"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 5:6",verse:"For the children of Israel walked forty years in the wilderness, till all the people that were men of war, which came out of Egypt, were consumed, because they obeyed not the voice of the LORD: unto whom the LORD sware that he would not shew them the land, which the LORD sware unto their fathers that he would give us, a land that floweth with milk and honey.",
   insight:"They missed the land for one reason: they would not listen. Hearing God's voice is the difference between wandering and inheriting."},
  {q:"Which generation had been circumcised, according to Joshua 5:5?", options:["All the people that came out of Egypt","The children born in the wilderness","The two spies","Rahab's household"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 5:5",verse:"Now all the people that came out were circumcised: but all the people that were born in the wilderness by the way as they came forth out of Egypt, them they had not circumcised.",
   insight:"The sign was kept at the Exodus, then neglected in the wandering. Covenant faithfulness can be lost one quiet generation at a time."},
  {q:"Whom did God raise up in the place of the uncircumcised fathers?", options:["Their children","Their servants","Strangers from Egypt","The mixed multitude"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 5:7",verse:"And their children, whom he raised up in their stead, them Joshua circumcised: for they were uncircumcised, because they had not circumcised them by the way.",
   insight:"God raises up the children to finish what the fathers forfeited. No generation's failure cancels God's purpose."},
  {q:"What did the people do after being circumcised, until they were whole?", options:["They abode in their places in the camp","They marched to Jericho","They offered sacrifices daily","They crossed back over Jordan"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 5:8",verse:"And it came to pass, when they had done circumcising all the people, that they abode in their places in the camp, till they were whole.",
   insight:"They stayed in camp until healed. Obedience sometimes means resting in place, not rushing to the next thing."},
  {q:"What does the LORD say He has done at Gilgal in Joshua 5:9?", options:["Rolled away the reproach of Egypt from off you","Given you the victory over Jericho","Forgiven all your sins","Made you a great nation"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 5:9",verse:"And the LORD said unto Joshua, This day have I rolled away the reproach of Egypt from off you. Wherefore the name of the place is called Gilgal unto this day.",
   insight:"The reproach of Egypt, the shame of slavery, is rolled away. God names places after the grace He shows there."},
  {q:"What does the name Gilgal mean in connection with Joshua 5:9?", options:["Rolling","Circle","Witness","Memorial"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 5:9",verse:"And the LORD said unto Joshua, This day have I rolled away the reproach of Egypt from off you. Wherefore the name of the place is called Gilgal unto this day.",
   insight:"Gilgal means rolling, from God rolling away reproach. Sometimes a place name is a whole theology."},
  {q:"On what day of the month did Israel keep the Passover at Gilgal?", options:["The fourteenth day of the month at even","The tenth day of the month","The first day of the month","The seventh day of the month"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 5:10",verse:"And the children of Israel encamped in Gilgal, and kept the passover on the fourteenth day of the month at even in the plains of Jericho.",
   insight:"The fourteenth day at evening, the exact Passover date from Egypt. The new generation keeps the old feast."},
  {q:"Where did Israel keep the Passover?", options:["In the plains of Jericho","In the wilderness","On Mount Ebal","At Shittim"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 5:10",verse:"And the children of Israel encamped in Gilgal, and kept the passover on the fourteenth day of the month at even in the plains of Jericho.",
   insight:"The Passover is kept in the plains of Jericho, in sight of the enemy city. Worship in Canaan begins before the conquest."},
  {q:"What did Israel eat the day after the Passover?", options:["Unleavened cakes, and parched corn of the old corn of the land","Manna and quails","Bread from the camp ovens","Fruit from the trees of Jericho"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 5:11",verse:"And they did eat of the old corn of the land on the morrow after the passover, unleavened cakes, and parched corn in the selfsame day.",
   insight:"They eat the land's own produce for the first time. The promise begins to feed them the day they taste it."},
  {q:"When did the manna cease?", options:["On the morrow after they had eaten of the old corn of the land","Forty days after the crossing","When they reached Jerusalem","After Jericho fell"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 5:12",verse:"And the manna ceased on the morrow after they had eaten of the old corn of the land; neither had the children of Israel manna any more; but they did eat of the fruit of the land of Canaan that year.",
   insight:"The manna stops the morning after they eat Canaan's corn. God's miraculous provision ends when ordinary blessing begins."},
  {q:"Near what city was Joshua when he saw the armed man?", options:["Jericho","Ai","Gilgal","Bethel"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 5:13",verse:"And it came to pass, when Joshua was by Jericho, that he lifted up his eyes and looked, and, behold, there stood a man over against him with his sword drawn in his hand: and Joshua went unto him, and said unto him, Art thou for us, or for our adversaries?",
   insight:"Joshua is by Jericho, scouting the first battle, when heaven's commander meets him. God meets strategists in the field."},
  {q:"What question does Joshua ask the man with the drawn sword?", options:["Art thou for us, or for our adversaries","What is thy name","Whence comest thou","What wilt thou have me do"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 5:13",verse:"And it came to pass, when Joshua was by Jericho, that he lifted up his eyes and looked, and, behold, there stood a man over against him with his sword drawn in his hand: and Joshua went unto him, and said unto him, Art thou for us, or for our adversaries?",
   insight:"'Art thou for us?' is the wrong question, and the answer corrects it. The issue is not whose side God is on, but whether we are on His."},
  {q:"How does the man answer Joshua?", options:["Nay; but as captain of the host of the LORD am I now come","I am for Israel","I am for Jericho","I am a traveler"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 5:14",verse:"And he said, Nay; but as captain of the host of the LORD am I now come. And Joshua fell on his face to the earth, and did worship, and said unto him, What saith my lord unto his servant?",
   insight:"'Nay' refuses both labels. Heaven's captain takes no sides; He takes command."},
  {q:"What does the captain of the LORD's host command Joshua to do?", options:["Loose thy shoe from off thy foot, for the place whereon thou standest is holy","Bow down seven times","Offer a lamb","Sound the trumpet"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 5:15",verse:"And the captain of the LORD’S host said unto Joshua, Loose thy shoe from off thy foot; for the place whereon thou standest is holy. And Joshua did so.",
   insight:"The same command given to Moses at the burning bush now comes to Joshua. Holy ground follows God's presence, even onto a battlefield."}
 ]}
]);
